{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 24, :comments ["<b>That place he called</b> etc. — meaning, the Holy One, blessed be He, beforehand wrote ״עַד נַחַל אֶשְׁכּוֹל״ on account of the future, for He declares the end from the beginning." "And His saying <b>which they cut from there</b> etc. — meaning: now, you might ask, were not many clusters cut from that place? Therefore He said, singling out this particular cluster after which the place was named: ״עַל אוֹדוֹת הָאֶשְׁכּוֹל״ etc. ״אֲשֶׁר כָּרְתוּ בְּנֵי יִשְׂרָאֵל״ — meaning, the entirety of Israel cut this cluster; and even though they were only twelve men, since they were emissaries of all Israel, it is as though all Israel cut it, along the lines of His saying (Exodus 12:6): ״וְשָׁחֲטוּ אֹתוֹ כֹּל קְהַל עֲדַת יִשְׂרָאֵל״."], :book :numbers, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 13, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T20:08:26.236865509Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}